Hi [Name], I did the initial analysis for ASP-9961. The main requirement is to improve logging around the existing retry mechanism so we can identify API failures properly in production.

My initial flow is:
API exception → RetryConfig / Retry handling → log exception + retry attempt/details → decide retry → retry if applicable.

I checked "RetryConfig.isRetryable()" in P2P Edge. Currently, it logs only the status code for "WebClientResponseException", while other exceptions are not logged.

For the solution, I see two possible approaches:

- @Recoverable approach → log the final exception once the retry attempts are exhausted.
- RetryListener approach → centrally log each retry attempt along with the exception details, which gives better visibility into the complete retry flow.

Since we don't currently have a RetryListener implemented, I’m leaning towards evaluating the listener approach along with enhancing "RetryConfig" where required, while keeping the existing retry behavior unchanged.